  "_schema": [
    "UNIFIED use-case registry (Track E) — SMART, not hardcoded. A use-case maps intent to",
    "CAPABILITY REQUIREMENTS (real attribute predicates from data/attributes/electronics.json), and",
    "the PRICE FLOOR is DERIVED from the cheapest in-catalog product meeting them (never a stored",
    "number — that drifts from reality the day prices change). budget_band_hint is ADVISORY ONLY",
    "(expectation-setting / cold-start); the catalog-derived floor is authoritative.",
    "HYBRID namespace: coarse use-case + baseline requirements + fine `variants` that ADD/OVERRIDE",
    "requirements (DRY). Brand/form premiums (Surface, Mac +30-50%) are EMERGENT — a shopper's brand",
    "preference is a filter, and the catalog prices it; nothing hardcodes the premium.",
    "requirement predicate form: {attr: [op, value]} with op in >=,<=,>,<,==,in."
